    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2ApjJf3fNB4nmVud6MqNpBi)_\n\n**Before:** in the browser graph and the SVG export of `sp-vulpea-hierarchy`, a box showed only the title, cut off with an ellipsis when it was long, and the file tags of the note were not shown.\n\n**After:** each box ends its title with the note's file tags, written `:tag1:tag2:` (muted in the browser), and the text wraps so all of it is visible. In the browser, boxes grow to fit their lines; in the SVG, labels wrap at `vulpea-hierarchy-wrap-width` characters (28 by default).\n\n**How:** the page measures text on a canvas and wraps it into `tspan` lines, and the layout now uses per-box heights. The Emacs side sends `tags` with each node and builds wrapped, escaped Graphviz labels (`vulpea-hierarchy--wrap`, `--label`, `--dot-label`). The literate doc is regenerated and tangles back byte for byte to the `.el` and `.html`. Tested with mock notes: JSON data, a JavaScript syntax check, a headless Chromium screenshot with a long title and four tags, and `dot` accepting a label with quotes. Not run against the real vault database.\n\nThis is the first of four stacked PRs; the next ones branch from it.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01YKB9W9Svzsc4PYxBD8qL9Q)_",
